  "authorNotes": "Nursery Maths. No Mohammadpur 2026 final exists for Nursery, so the guide is the Mohammadpur Annual 2025 Nursery Maths paper (MP_OTHER). Its 8 written questions are the same 8 rows as the Sylhet syllabus, in the same order, and all numbers are inside the 2026 Nursery Maths books (1–50), so Q1–Q6 are reused unchanged: Bangla 11–25, English 36–50, the ৪১–৫০ and 11–20 ordering sets (both also printed in the book, pp.48), the Number/সংখ্যা pairs and the before/after items. Q7 and Q8 had only 5 pictures each in Mohammadpur (5 marks each); the Sylhet rows need 15 each, so the 5 Mohammadpur pictures are kept and 10 new picture items were added to each, all counts between 1 and 20 so the child can count them. Things the owner should know: (a) The counts in the Mohammadpur Q8 pictures were read from a photocopy (phones 18, turtles 6, flowers 11, cups 14, apples 9) — the Office should draw each picture with exactly the count written in [ছবি: …]. (b) Row 5 'Number ও সংখ্যা মিলিয়ে লেখ' is marked 'matching' in the syllabus, but Mohammadpur and the book (p.49) do it as 'write the other form next to it' (4 → ৪, ৯ → 9), so it is drafted that way, with no match column. (c) Q7 asks for a সংখ্যা (Bangla digits); Mohammadpur's wording asked for a Number — the reviewer may want to accept either. (d) Duration 2 hours is copied from the Mohammadpur paper. (e) Mohammadpur also had dictation 10, oral 5 and cleanliness 5; the Sylhet table has none of these, so they are left out. Page numbers in bookRef are the printed page numbers of the 2026 Nursery Maths books (Bangla and English versions share the same page layout)."
}
